#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Report which service and region host a site, separating edge from origin.

Reads only what a browser reads: DNS, the TLS certificate, one HTTP response and
the assets that response links. Vendor and region are the promise; a project or
account id is reported when the site happens to expose one and never guessed.

Edge and network are printed as separate facts because both are true at once.
Netlify runs on AWS Global Accelerator, so `edge: Netlify` and `network: AS16509
Amazon` describe one site correctly and collapsing them into a single verdict is
wrong whichever one wins.
"""

